      "created_at": "2016-04-11T12:53:56Z",
      "updated_at": "2016-04-11T12:53:56Z",
      "body": "Thanks for fast answer.\nOK, after asking partner1 again, I have indeed to correct me: both have seen a link! Sorry.\n\nBut why is this connected with privacy issues?\nIs clicking the link to display it in a browser less intruding than letting Monal download it and displaying it? Is this a Monal-issue or an iOS specific or even a general one (which would mean you claim that Conversations make a \"serious privacy issue\" with in-line display of images....which I would doubt!)\nIs IP adress during XMPP conversations not anyway an anavoidable metadata (without TOR etc)?\n\nIn terms of privacy......I would say until Monal does not support OMEMO, it is a step to far to care about privacy with in-line images. Wouldn't you agree?\n\nThus, I strongly ask the feature of in-line displaying (opt-in or not) of images!\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
