      "created_at": "2016-04-11T13:02:45Z",
      "updated_at": "2016-04-11T13:02:45Z",
      "body": "In a one on one conversation, both people are talking to a server and not to each other so neither knows the others ip. The way the online image is detected, it makes a http head call automatically for every link to check if it is an image. This head call connects to a server automatically . Basically, if I wanted to know where someone was I would send a url unique to them. They don't even have to click it, just receiving the message would let me look in my logs to see their ip and location. At least with a click the recipient is aware that something is happening.  If you trust the other party it's not a big deal, receiving a random message, it's a problem. \n",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
